# The system groups rubyfunk ships (sysusers.d(5)). pacman and rpm apply this file on install;
# packaging/linux/post-install.sh, the deb client postinst and the Steam Deck scripts run
# systemd-sysusers on it.
#
# rubyfunk owns the usbip vhci attach/detach nodes (60-rubyfunk.rules) and is the group
# pf-dm-helper's polkit action authorizes. It is not 'input': writing attach materialises an
# arbitrary emulated USB device. Nobody is added; joining is the opt-in.
g rubyfunk -
# The door's own group (rubyfunk-door.service). The door runs as the `rubyfunk` user, whose
# primary group is this one, so it never holds the attach nodes or passes pf-dm-helper.
g rubyfunk-door -
# Members may start the update units through polkit (49-rubyfunk-*update.rules). Shipped empty.
g rubyfunk-update -
